      "html": "† I. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">חָם</span></big>  <strong>nome próprio pessoal masculino</strong> e <strong>de lugar (</strong>cf. sabeu <span dir=\"rtl\">חם</span> Hal<sup>243</sup><strong>)</strong>—𝔊 Χαμ:—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <strong>Cam</strong>, segundo filho de Noé <a data-ref=\"Genesis 5:32\" href=\"/Genesis.5.32\">Gn 5:32</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 6:10\" href=\"/Genesis.6.10\">6:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 7:13\" href=\"/Genesis.7.13\">7:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 9:18\" href=\"/Genesis.9.18\">9:18</a><sup>(×2)</sup> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 1:4\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.1.4\">1 Ch 1:4</a>; chamado pai de Canaã <a data-ref=\"Genesis 9:22\" href=\"/Genesis.9.22\">Gn 9:22</a> e de vários povos <a data-ref=\"Genesis 10:1\" href=\"/Genesis.10.1\">10:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 10:6\" href=\"/Genesis.10.6\">6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 10:20\" href=\"/Genesis.10.20\">20</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 1:8\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.1.8\">1 Ch 1:8</a>, cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן־חָם הַיֹּשְׁבִים שָׁם</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 4:40\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.4.40\">4:40</a>; esses povos eram habitantes de terras meridionais, ou estavam histórica ou politicamente relacionados com tais habitantes; ver <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, כּוּשׁ\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_כּוּשׁ\">כּוּשׁ</a>, <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, כְּנַ֫עַן²\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_כְּנַ֫עַן²\">כְּנַעַן</a>, <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, אֵבֶל מִצְרַיִם\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_אֵבֶל מִצְרַיִם\">מִצְרַיִם</a>, <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, פּוּט\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_פּוּט\">פּוּט</a>, etc.<br><strong>2.</strong>  em Salmos tardios, nome (coletivo) dos egípcios:—<span dir=\"rtl\">אָֽהֳלֵי־ח׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 78:51\" href=\"/Psalms.78.51\">ψ 78:51</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ־ח׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 105:23\" href=\"/Psalms.105.23\">105:23</a>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 105:27\" href=\"/Psalms.105.27\">27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 106:22\" href=\"/Psalms.106.22\">106:22</a> (todos ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מִצְרַיִם</span>, exceto <a data-ref=\"Psalms 105:27\" href=\"/Psalms.105.27\">105:27</a>).—Quanto à significação histórica e às tentativas de etimologia, ver Di <sup>Gen. ed. 6, chap. 10, especially pp. 165, 168 f.</sup>, Hom <sup>SV i. 427</sup> Bu<sup>Urg. 323</sup> Wiedemann<sup>Ägypt. Gesch. i. 22</sup>.",
