      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">חֶמְאָה</span></big>  <strong>substantivo feminino: coalhada</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">ח׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 18:8\" href=\"/Genesis.18.8\">Gn 18:8</a> + 6 vezes; = <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵמָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 29:6\" href=\"/Job.29.6\">Jb 29:6</a>; construto <span dir=\"rtl\">חֶמְאַח</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 32:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.32.14\">Dt 32:14</a>; <em>coalhada, leite coalhado</em>, moderno <em>leben</em>; quanto ao modo de preparar <em>lebben</em>, agitando o leite num odre de leite azedo, ver Doughty<sup>Arabic Des. i. 221, 263; ii. 304, etc.</sup> Thomson <sup>Land and Book ii. 418</sup>. Ver também ARSK<sup>Ency. Bib. Milk</sup>. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִיץ חָלָב יוֹצִיא ח׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 30:33\" href=\"/Proverbs.30.33\">Pr 30:33</a>, alhures associado a <span dir=\"rtl\">חָלָב</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 18:8\" href=\"/Genesis.18.8\">Gn 18:8</a> (J) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 32:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.32.14\">Dt 32:14</a> (poema; <span dir=\"rtl\">חֶמְאַת בָּקָר וַחֲלֵב צֹאן</span>), <a data-ref=\"Judges 5:25\" href=\"/Judges.5.25\">Ju 5:25</a> (onde é servido <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּסֵפֶל אַדִּירִים</span>, ver <a data-ref=\"BDB, סֵ֫פֶל\" href=\"/BDB,_סֵ֫פֶל\", dir=\"rtl\">ספל</a>); com <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּבַשׁ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:29\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.29\">2 S 17:29</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 7:15\" href=\"/Isaiah.7.15\">Is 7:15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 7:22\" href=\"/Isaiah.7.22\">22</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">נַחֲלֵי דבשׁ וח׳</span>, figura de abundância <a data-ref=\"Job 20:17\" href=\"/Job.20.17\">Jb 20:17</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">בִּרְחֹץ הֲלִיכַי בְּחֵמָ֑ה</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 29:6\" href=\"/Job.29.6\">Jb 29:6</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">צוּר יָצוּק פַּלְגֵי־שָֽׁמֶן׃</span>). <span dir=\"rtl\">מַחֲמָאֹת</span>.",
